    "summary": "This '34 Ford highboy was purchased by the seller as in-progress build and was recently completed using a Henry Ford 1934 pickup cab and frame, along with a shortened reproduction bed. Powering the pickup is a 283ci V8, which is topped by an Edelbrock intake manifold and carburetor and linked to a three-speed automatic and a 10-bolt rear end with a Positraction differential. The truck rides on whitewalls mounted on chromed 15\" steelies, and it has a Super Bell drop axle, a four-bar front setup, a four-link rear end, Bilstein chromed shocks, and a transverse leaf spring along with a Vega steering box and GM-sourced front discs. The Washington Blue paintwork is complemented by a wood-lined bed and white upholstery, and the pickup is further equipped with lake-style headers with cutouts. The driver is provided a three-spoke wheel, a Lokar shifter, a hidden Bluetooth audio system, and Stewart-Warner gauges. Purchased by the seller in 2025, this highboy pickup is now offered with removed louvered hood panels, records, and a Texas title in the seller's name listing it as a 1934 Ford.",
